                    <desc type="abstract" xml:lang="en" source="#bib2534-4" corresp="http://syriaca.org/geo">Eastern capital under multiple dynasties including the Tang, major urban center near Chang’an in the North China Plain. It operated at times as a secondary imperial capital, reflecting shifting political and administrative priorities within the empire. A newly excavated funerary stele dated to 815 from Luoyang provides late Tang evidence of Christian communities continuing to exist beyond the primary capital.</desc>
                    <desc xml:lang="en" resp="http://syriaca.org">A capital of the Tang dynasty in modern Henan province in <placeName ref="http://syriaca.org/place/472">China</placeName>.</desc>
